 "idea": {
  "id": "vix_fear_buy",
  "family": "volatility",
  "title": "Buy the index for a few days when fear spikes",
  "why": "When near-dated fear (VIX) rises above three-month fear (VIX3M), or jumps well above its own recent level, investors are paying up for protection and dealers are short of risk capacity; the days after have paid more than usual for holding shares. The risk is that the few times it fails are crashes.",
  "source": "Whaley 2009; Nagel 2012; common practitioner rule",
